hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27676","Haddathana Ya'qub, he said: My father narrated to me from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Nuh ibn Hakim al-Thaqafi, who was a reciter of the Qur'an, narrated to me from a man of Banu Urwah ibn Mas'ud called Dawud, whom Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had borne, from Layla bint Qanif al-Thaqafiyyah, she said: I was among those who washed Umm Kulthum, daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at her death, and the first of what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave us was the waist-wrapper, then the dress, then the headcover, then the sheet, then she was wrapped afterwards in the last garment. She said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was at the door with her shroud, handing it to us garment by garment."
